      <div class="paper flow" id="task">
        <p class="note-label">Your coding task: count the votes</p>
        <p>Room 1 is choosing its class president. Each vote is a name on a slip of paper. On the board, you would write each name once and add a mark beside it for every vote. A map does the same: name → number of votes.</p>
        <p>Finish the loop in <code>countVotes</code> in about 5 lines where it says YOUR CODE. You need only three methods from <Peek label="Part 2" title="From Part 2 · Map methods" html={methodsPeek} />: <code>containsKey</code>, <code>get</code>, and <code>put</code>. The map is a <a href="#map-kinds">TreeMap</a>, so the names print sorted and your output can match the expected comments exactly. Run it: each printed line must match its expected comment.</p>
        <pre class="code"><code set:html={hiN(taskCode)} /></pre>
